{"kind":"request","text":"BO5: views as code. Fifth slice of the boundary-objects design note (notes/2026-10-28-boundary-objects-in-use.md, section 9, landed 25930f62), child of request bc4aa093. After BO2.\n\nScope, as the note's slice list states it:\n1. A view whose text is code, run in the sandbox domain (the application sandbox Worker on the inguz.space zone) over the sources its about names, with the same way to write an act as a declared view: the host shows the exact act, signs it on the member's action alone, and refuses an act the member's grants or memberships do not allow.\n2. The code view reaches nothing but its sources: no other room, no other note, no network beyond the host's view session.\n3. Witness W5 (a view as code): W2 again with B's view written as code and run in the sandbox domain; the same outcomes as W2, and the host's record shows every act the code view wrote and who signed it.\n\nNot in this slice: anything of BO1 to BO4.","body":{"conditions":"A view whose text is code runs in the sandbox domain over the sources its about names and nothing else; every act it writes is shown by the host and signed on the member's action alone, and acts beyond the member's grants are refused; witness W5 recorded with immutable evidence; gate green.","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}